                        </div>
                        <div class="RelativeElement Z10Element MarginXAutoElement MaxWidth7XL PaddingX6Element LargePaddingX8Element">
                              <div class="MarginXAutoElement MaxWidth2XL TextCenterElement LargeMarginXZeroElement LargeMaxWidthNoneElement">
                                    <h2 class="Text3XLElement FontBoldElement TrackingTightElement TextGray900Element SmallText4XLElement">A design perspective shaped around your home</h2>
                                    <p class="MarginTop6Element TextLargeElement Leading8Element TextGray600Element">Good interior design starts with questions, not assumptions. What matters most in the space? How do its rooms support daily routines? Which details already feel personal, and what would you like to change? Considering these points helps create a more relevant direction before visual choices are made.</p>
                                    <p class="MarginTop6Element TextLargeElement Leading8Element TextGray600Element">
                                          There is no single measure that defines a successful interior, and no one set of choices suits every household. Blueprint Living's approach is expressed through connected design considerations: how space is used, how a visual direction is developed, how light and materials are understood, and how personal character remains part of the result. These are principles for exploring a home, not claimed project totals or guaranteed outcomes.
                                    </p>
                              </div>
                              <div class="MarginTop16Element GridElement GridColumnsOneElement Gap8Element SmallGridColumns2Element LargeGridColumns4Element">
                                    <div class="FlexElement FlexColumnElement ItemsCenterElement Padding6Element BGWhiteElement RoundedLargeElement ShadowLargeElement TransformElement TransitionTransformElement HoverRotate2Element HoverScale105Element">
                                          <dd class="Text5XLElement FontBoldElement TextPurple900Element">01</dd>
                                          <dt class="MarginTop4Element TextBaseElement Leading7Element TextGray600Element">Begin with the people and routines that shape the home.</dt>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="FlexElement FlexColumnElement ItemsCenterElement Padding6Element BGWhiteElement RoundedLargeElement ShadowLargeElement TransformElement TransitionTransformElement HoverNegativeRotate2Element HoverScale105Element">
                                          <dd class="Text5XLElement FontBoldElement TextPurple900Element">02</dd>
                                          <dt class="MarginTop4Element TextBaseElement Leading7Element TextGray600Element">Consider colour, materials and furnishings as a connected whole.</dt>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="FlexElement FlexColumnElement ItemsCenterElement Padding6Element BGWhiteElement RoundedLargeElement ShadowLargeElement TransformElement TransitionTransformElement HoverRotate1Element HoverScale105Element">
                                          <dd class="Text5XLElement FontBoldElement TextPurple900Element">03</dd>
                                          <dt class="MarginTop4Element TextBaseElement Leading7Element TextGray600Element">Take room proportions, movement and light into account.</dt>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="FlexElement FlexColumnElement ItemsCenterElement Padding6Element BGWhiteElement RoundedLargeElement ShadowLargeElement TransformElement TransitionTransformElement HoverNegativeRotate1Element HoverScale105Element">
                                          <dd class="Text5XLElement FontBoldElement TextPurple900Element">04</dd>
                                          <dt class="MarginTop4Element TextBaseElement Leading7Element TextGray600Element">Make space for personal taste and meaningful details.</dt>
                                    </div>
                              </div>
                        </div>
                  </div>
            </div>
            <div id="bqoiq">
                  <div class="BGWhiteElement BorderYElement">
                        <div class="MarginXAutoElement MaxWidth7XL PaddingX6Element PaddingY16Element SmallPaddingY24Element LargePaddingX8Element">
                              <h2 class="Text2XLElement FontBoldElement Leading10Element TrackingTightElement TextGray900Element">Frequently asked questions</h2>
                              <p class="MarginTop6Element MaxWidth2XL TextBaseElement Leading7Element TextGray600Element">
                                    Interior design is personal, and the right starting point depends on the home, the people who use it and the decisions they need to make. These answers offer general guidance about the design approach described on this page. They do not confirm specific services, prices, timelines or availability; please contact Blueprint Living directly for details relevant to your project.
                              </p>
                              <div class="MarginTop20Element">
                                    <dl class="SpaceY16Element SmallGridElement SmallGridColumns2Element SmallGapX6Element SmallGapY16Element SmallSpaceYZeroElement LargeGapX10Element">
                                          <div>
                                                <dt class="TextBaseElement FontSemiBoldElement Leading7Element TextGray900Element">What does interior design involve?</dt>
                                                <dd class="MarginTop2Element TextBaseElement Leading7Element TextGray600Element">Interior design can involve considering the layout, colours, materials, lighting and furnishings of a space. The appropriate scope depends on the home and the decisions being explored.</dd>
                                          </div>
                                          <div>
                                                <dt class="TextBaseElement FontSemiBoldElement Leading7Element TextGray900Element">Do I need a complete plan before making contact?</dt>
                                                <dd class="MarginTop2Element TextBaseElement Leading7Element TextGray600Element">No complete plan is needed to begin a conversation. It can be helpful to share what you would like to change, what already works and any practical considerations you have.</dd>
                                          </div>
                                          <div>
                                                <dt class="TextBaseElement FontSemiBoldElement Leading7Element TextGray900Element">Can the design reflect my personal style?</dt>
                                                <dd class="MarginTop2Element TextBaseElement Leading7Element TextGray600Element">A considered design direction should take your preferences, routines and existing belongings into account. Specific design options depend on the details of your home and your discussions with the company.</dd>
                                          </div>
                                          <div>
                                                <dt class="TextBaseElement FontSemiBoldElement Leading7Element TextGray900Element">How can I find out about availability or project details?</dt>
                                                <dd class="MarginTop2Element TextBaseElement Leading7Element TextGray600Element">Contact Blueprint Living directly to ask about current availability, project scope, fees and any other details. This page does not make claims about those terms.</dd>
                                          </div>
                                    </dl>
                              </div>
                        </div>
                  </div>
